From c62f63236a406654ea05037eae3b63bfc62f2c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [MNT] defaultenv: mnt-reform2-rk3588: add disp-reset init script

Send the 'r' SPI command to the RP2040 system controller at barebox
startup to pulse the panel hardware RESX line (PIN_DISP_RESET, GPIO 2)
before autoboot.

The RP2040 pulses RESX on cold boot but not on warm reboot. Without this
pulse, the Wisecoco V2 panel (ER88477) gets a blank screen because DSI
init races against an uninitialized panel. The JDI V1 panel may also
benefit from a clean reset on warm reboot.

The reform2_lpc protocol (matching the Linux reform2_lpc.c driver) requires
two separate SPI transactions with a 50ms gap between them. The RP2040
processes commands in a timer interrupt after the first transaction's CS
deasserts, then fills its TX FIFO before the second transaction clocks out
the response. A combined write+read in one transaction gives the RP2040 no
time to respond and produces all-zero reads.

Command bytes: { 0xb5, 0x72, 0x01, 0xc6 }
  0xb5 = LPC magic, 0x72 = 'r' (display reset), 0x01 = trigger,
  0xc6 = XOR checksum. Response is 8 bytes (ignored); RESX pulse occurs
  after the response is sent, so the trailing 50ms covers both the 20ms
  pulse and panel stabilization time.

Depends on: RP2040 firmware with 'r' command support
            spi-gpio node in DTS (patch 0004)
---
 .../defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/init/disp-reset    | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/init/disp-reset

diff --git a/arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/init/disp-reset b/arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/init/disp-reset
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..000000000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/init/disp-reset
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Pulse panel hardware RESX via the RP2040 system controller before autoboot.
+#
+# The RP2040 owns PIN_DISP_RESET (GPIO 2) and pulses it on cold boot, but not
+# on warm reboot. The 'r' SPI command triggers a 20ms active-low pulse, giving
+# the panel a clean reset regardless of how barebox was entered.
+#
+# The reform2_lpc protocol requires two separate SPI transactions with a 50ms
+# gap between them. Write and read must be separate calls: the RP2040 processes
+# the command in a timer interrupt after the first transaction completes, then
+# fills its TX FIFO with the response before the second transaction clocks it
+# out. A combined write+read in one transaction leaves no time for this and
+# the RP2040 sends zeros.
+#
+# Command: { 0xb5, 'r'=0x72, arg1=0x01, checksum=0xc6 }
+# checksum = 0xb5 ^ 0x72 ^ 0x01 = 0xc6
+# Response: 8 bytes (ignored); RESX pulse occurs after the response is sent.
+spi -b 0 -c 0 -m 1 -f 1000000 0xb5 0x72 0x01 0xc6
+msleep 50
+spi -b 0 -c 0 -m 1 -f 1000000 -r 8
+msleep 50
--
